An upbeat song filled the pod.

14
00:01:06.712 --> 00:01:10.456
"Satisfactory choice?" the computer asked.

15
00:01:10.457 --> 00:01:30.401
"Yes! I love this song!" Ally jumped up to dance around.

16
00:01:30.402 --> 00:01:37.281
When the song ended, she sighed. "I guess it's time to get to work."

17
00:01:37.282 --> 00:01:40.845
"It's long past time," the computer said. Ally

18
00:01:40.846 --> 00:01:45.132
scowled. "Are you going to start nagging me too? Besides,

19
00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:50.014
if you're so smart, why can't you fix the comm device yourself?" "Repair

20
00:01:50.015 --> 00:01:54.225
of communication devices is beyond my capabilities." The

21
00:01:54.226 --> 00:01:59.482
computer's lights dimmed as it put itself to sleep. "That's

22
00:01:59.483 --> 00:02:04.881
fine," Ally mumbled. "I don't need your help or anyone else's. I'll

23
00:02:04.882 --> 00:02:08.302
have this comm device working in no time." She

24
00:02:08.303 --> 00:02:13.227
took another sip of juba juice and sat down to work. ***

25
00:02:13.228 --> 00:02:19.471
A short while later, Ally had taken the comm device apart, and all the pieces sat in front of her.

26
00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.907
She pushed her tentacles out of her face.

27
00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:29.088
"That wasn't very hard. And I found the problem. The fuse was blown. Now

28
00:02:29.089 --> 00:02:32.813
all I have to do is put the device back together." The

29
