Alpha ," Ally replied, "but I took it apart, so I can totally put it back together."

31
00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.329
She snorted. "My parents will be sorry they called me irresponsible."

32
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:57.043
The computer made a noise that sounded like "Hmm."

33
00:02:57.044 --> 00:03:01.485
*** Before long, Ally had finished reassembling the

34
00:03:01.486 --> 00:03:06.278
device. "See, Alpha ?" She proudly flipped

35
00:03:06.279 --> 00:03:08.812
her tentacles. "I told you I didn't need

36
00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:13.585
the manual." "Standing by for test of communication device," the

37
00:03:13.586 --> 00:03:19.023
computer said. "Here we go!" Ally turned the device on, expecting it to

38
00:03:19.024 --> 00:03:27.610
light up. But nothing happened. She tried again.

39
00:03:27.611 --> 00:03:32.116
Still nothing. "That's funny," Ally murmured. "I don't know what's

40
00:03:32.117 --> 00:03:37.517
wrong." "Scanning area." The computer clicked and

41
00:03:37.518 --> 00:03:42.601
clacked. "Detecting nanochip receiver on the floor. Repeat, detecting

42
00:03:42.602 --> 00:03:48.231
nanochip—" "I heard you the first time!" Ally checked the floor by her

43
00:03:48.232 --> 00:03:53.212
feet. The computer was right—a part from the device was lying there.

44
00:03:53.213 --> 00:03:57.420
"Oops." She didn't want to admit it out loud, but it was time to consult the

45
00:03:57.421 --> 00:04:02.560
manual. As Ally reached across the dashboard to grab the tablet, her arm knocked into the juba

46
00:04:02.561 --> 00:04:07.367
juice. The bottle tipped, spilling sticky juice all over the manual and the

47
00:04:07.368 --> 00:04:10.993
dashboard. The tablet sparked, while the dashboard fizzled and

48
00:04:10.994 --> 00:04:14.839
popped. "Oh no!" Ally cried. "What have I

49
00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:17.678
done?" "Sensors indicate you spilled juba juice, and the—"

50
00:04:17.679 --> 00:04:23.094
"I know what I did!" Ally snapped. "I need to know how to undo it!"

51
